          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "18.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The sum of the 4th and 8th terms of an AP is 24 and the sum of the 6th and 10th terms is 44. Find the first three terms of the AP."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.203,
            0.902,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "19.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Subba Rao started work in 1995 at an annual salary of ` 5000 and received an increment of ` 200 each year. In which year did his income reach ` 7000?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.244,
            0.901,
            0.282
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "20.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Ramkali saved ` 5 in the first week of a year and then increased her weekly savings by ` 1.75. If in the nth week, her weekly savings become ` 20.75, find n."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.294,
            0.472,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.4 Sum of First n Terms of an AP"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.321,
            0.442,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us consider the situation again given in Section 5.1 in which Shakila put ` 100 into her daughter’s money box when she was one year old, ` 150 on her second birthday, ` 200 on her third birthday and will continue in the same way. How much money will be collected in the money box by the time her daughter is 21 years old?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.521,
            0.314,
            0.802,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.521,
                0.314,
                0.802,
                0.51
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.52,
            0.902,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here, the amount of money (in `) put in the money box on her first, second, third, fourth . . . birthday were respectively 100, 150, 200, 250, . . . till her 21st birthday. To find the total amount in the money box on her 21st birthday, we will have to write each of the 21 numbers in the list above and then add them up. Don’t you think it would be a tedious and time consuming process? Can we make the process shorter? This would be possible if we can find a method for getting this sum. Let us see."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.642,
            0.903,
            0.719
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We consider the problem given to Gauss (about whom you read in Chapter 1), to solve when he was just 10 years old. He was asked to find the sum of the positive integers from 1 to 100. He immediately replied that the sum is 5050. Can you guess how did he do? He wrote :"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.723,
            0.562,
            0.741
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "S = 1 + 2 + 3 + \\cdots + 99 + 100"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.747,
            0.491,
            0.765
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "And then, reversed the numbers to write"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.77,
            0.559,
            0.788
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "S = 100 + 99 + \\cdots + 3 + 2 + 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.795,
            0.343,
            0.814
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Adding these two, he got"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.245,
            0.817,
            0.871,
            0.86
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}2 S  = & (100 + 1) + (99 + 2) + \\ldots + (3 + 98) + (2 + 99) + (1 + 100) \\\\= & 101 + 101 + \\ldots + 101 + 101 \\quad (100  times )\\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.882,
            0.135,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.252,
            0.867,
            0.685,
            0.908
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_14_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{S}=\\frac{100 \\times 101}{2}=5050, \\mathrm{i.e., the sum}=5050."
        },
